<ns0:exercise xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167836409832" class="material-set-2">
<ns0:problem id="fs-id1167833386164">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167833386167">The number of unwatched shows in Sylvia’s DVR is 85. This number grows by 20 unwatched shows per week. The function <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>N</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>t</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>85</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>20</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>t</ns1:mi></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> represents the relation between the number of unwatched shows, <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">N</ns0:emphasis>, and the time, <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">t</ns0:emphasis>, measured in weeks.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167824737629"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> Determine the independent and dependent variable.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836697913"><ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> Find <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>N</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>4</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> Explain what this result means</ns0:para>
</ns0:problem>
<ns0:solution id="fs-id1167833378063">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167832935494"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">t</ns0:emphasis> IND; <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">N</ns0:emphasis> DEP<ns0:newline /><ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>N</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>4</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>165</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> the number of unwatched shows in Sylvia’s DVR at the fourth week. </ns0:para>
</ns0:solution>
</ns0:exercise>
